abstract: >-
  A complete 7-step computational pipeline for detecting and
  quantifying dredging vessel activities using Automatic
  Identification System (AIS) tracking data, and estimating
  the resulting carbon perturbation via an Ocean Circulation
  Inverse Model (OCIM). The pipeline combines Isolation Forest
  outlier detection, Gaussian Mixture Model and DBSCAN clustering
  for vessel behaviour classification, global grid computation of
  swept-volume ratios and dredging intensity (f_i), seabed
  lithology integration from dbSEABED, carbon release index (C_ri)
  calculation from Atwood et al. (2024) benthic carbon stocks, and
  remapping of dredge-induced carbon fluxes (Jdredge) to the
  OCIM2-48L transport matrix for steady-state pCO2 perturbation
  modelling. Uncertainty is propagated via 500-iteration Monte Carlo
  simulation following GUM (JCGM 100:2008). Target journal:
  Limnology and Oceanography: Methods (Wiley).
